Task 5 actual voice-runtime milestone

Implementation:
- CallHandler now constructs NativeFlowAdapter for explicitly selected,
  published native graphs rather than the pilot-only adapter. It selects the
  configured FLOW by native_flow_tool_id while preserving unrelated assigned
  tools, uses the authoritative published FlowVersion, and retains the
  call-owned session/property/identity fences.
- The actual voice host creates a voice-scoped NativeActionRunner only for
  graphs that contain action nodes; function-mapper end/transfer primitives
  handle terminal speech, playback marks, and carrier work.
- Deferred transfer outcomes update the matching pending native terminal.
  Carrier acceptance remains pending and is not reported as a connected human;
  failed outcomes settle as terminal_failed. End speech remains owned by the
  existing mapper primitive, not duplicated by the adapter.
- Native Flow globalPrompt is admitted and included in actual provider context.
  Unknown saved graph fields still fail before pipeline creation.
- Native multi-tool development fixtures now use valid scoped IDs and stable
  per-store sessions, so scoped native action execution is tested without
  broadening real I/O or weakening lifecycle guards.

